<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Experiment Details</h3>

<section id="A1.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.1.1 </span>Composition of Multi-Guidance Pool</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Main Experiments Teachers (4 LongCoTs).</span> The four primary teacher models were selected for their strong long chain-of-thought (LongCoT) reasoning capabilities:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AceReason-Nemotron-1.1-7B</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2025d)</a></cite>: A 7B parameter model from NVIDIA, developed by applying a combination of Supervised Fine-Tuning (SFT) and multi-stage Reinforcement Learning (RL) on Qwen2.5-Math-7B.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al. (2025)</a></cite>: A 7B parameter model created by DeepSeek-AI through knowledge distillation. It uses the powerful DeepSeek-R1 as the teacher model to fine-tune a Qwen2.5-Math-7B student model, transferring its advanced reasoning capabilities.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">OpenR1-Qwen-7B</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hugging Face (2025)</a></cite>: A 7B parameter fully open reproduction of early DeepSeek-R1 capabilities, developed by fine-tuning a Qwen2.5-Math-7B-Instruct base model on the extensive OpenR1-220k-Math dataset.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen3-8B</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team (2025)</a></cite>: A 8B parameter powerful base model from Alibaba Cloud’s Qwen3 series. It is designed for balanced performance in both complex reasoning and general conversational tasks. We utilize its ”thinking mode” for main experiments.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Discussion Experiments Teachers (“R1 only”, “4 ShortCoTs”).</span> For the ablation study on teacher composition, we included additional models representing different capabilities and reasoning styles:</p>
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DeepSeek-R1</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al. (2025)</a></cite>: The 677B parameter powerful, proprietary reasoning model from DeepSeek-AI used as a single-teacher baseline. It was developed through a sophisticated multi-stage pipeline involving both RL and SFT.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen2.5-Math-7B-Ins</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al. (2024)</a></cite>: An 7B parameter instruction-tuned model from Alibaba Cloud, specifically optimized for mathematical reasoning tasks using both Chain-of-Thought and Tool-integrated Reasoning data.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen2.5-Math-7B-Oat-Zero</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2025c)</a></cite>: A 7B parameter model derived from Qwen2.5-Math-7B through a pure reinforcement learning process (similar to R1-Zero), which aims to unlock reasoning capabilities without relying on expert demonstrations.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SynLogic-7B</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2025a)</a></cite>: A 7B parameter model built on the Qwen2.5-7B-Base model and enhanced with reinforcement learning (RL) using the specialized SynLogic dataset fine-tuned specifically on the SynLogic dataset, specifically for advanced logical reasoning.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen3-8B</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team (2025)</a></cite>: A 8B parameter powerful base model from Alibaba Cloud’s Qwen3 series. It is designed for balanced performance in both complex reasoning and general conversational tasks. We utilize its ”no thinking mode” for discussion experiments.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.1.2 </span>Dataset Construction Details</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure a fair comparison across all experimental settings, particularly the analysis of different teacher compositions (the results of which are in Table <a href="#S4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 4.4 Ablation Study and Discussions ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ More Than One Teacher: Adaptive Multi-Guidance Policy Optimization for Diverse Exploration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), our datasets were constructed through a rigorous, multi-stage process designed to maintain a consistent set of questions for all models.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="A1.I3" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Source Data:</span> We began with the 10,000 question-answer (QA) pairs from the OpenR1-Math-46k-8192 dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yan et al. (2025)</a></cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Per-Composition Data Curation:</span> For each teacher composition group defined in our study, we curated a corresponding set of demonstrations.</p>
<ul id="A1.I3.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A1.I3.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For compositions involving our selected LongCoT or ShortCoT models, we executed a full generation pipeline:</p>
<ul id="A1.I3.i2.I1.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A1.I3.i2.I1.i1.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.I1.i1.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.I1.i1.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i2.I1.i1.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Generation:</span> Each teacher model within the group was prompted to generate 8 distinct reasoning paths for every question.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2.I1.i1.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.I1.i1.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.I1.i1.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i2.I1.i1.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Verification:</span> All generated paths were evaluated for correctness using Math-Verify <span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
                                  <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
                                  
                                  
                                  
                                https://github.com/huggingface/Math-Verify</span></span></span>, and incorrect responses were discarded.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2.I1.i1.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.I1.i1.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.I1.i1.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i2.I1.i1.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Selection:</span> For each question, if a teacher produced multiple correct paths, we retained only its shortest correct path to ensure conciseness.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the baseline “R1 only” composition, we directly used the high-quality demonstrations already provided in the source dataset, as they were originally generated by DeepSeek-R1.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dataset Unification via Intersection:</span> After curating data for every teacher composition, we obtained multiple candidate datasets. To create a unified set of questions for all our experiments, we took the <span id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">intersection of the question sets</span> from all these candidate datasets. This crucial step ensures that for every question in our final dataset, there is at least one correct demonstration available from every teacher composition group we tested.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Final RL Dataset Curation:</span> The intersection process yielded our final RL dataset of <span id="A1.I3.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8,491</span> unique QA pairs. The <span id="A1.I3.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Multi-Guidance Pool (<math id="A1.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{G}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span> for each question is therefore dynamic: for any given experiment (<span id="A1.I3.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span>, training with the “4 LongCoTs” composition), the pool for a question contains the correct demonstrations <span id="A1.I3.i4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">only from those teachers in the group who successfully solved it</span>. Thus, the number of demonstrations per question can range from one to the total number of teachers in the composition.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SFT dataset</span>, used for our main baseline comparison, was then created from the complete set of demonstrations generated by our primary “4 LongCoTs” teacher composition. By treating each of the 8,491 questions and its corresponding correct teacher demonstrations as individual training instances, we expanded the data into a comprehensive SFT dataset of <span id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">32,252</span> pairs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.1.3 </span>System Prompt and Reward Function Design</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure consistent and automated evaluation for both our reward function and comprehension score (<math id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>), we used a standardized concise system prompt for all models. The prompt instructs the model to provide a step-by-step reasoning process and enclose the final answer in &lt;answer&gt;&lt;/answer&gt;tags consistent with the <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al. (2025b)</a></cite>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="139.41" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 139.41" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,139.41) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#606060;" fill="#606060" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 133.51 C 0 136.77 2.64 139.41 5.91 139.41 L 544.09 139.41 C 547.36 139.41 550 136.77 550 133.51 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 115.45 L 548.03 115.45 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 124.05)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">System Prompt</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:6.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="89.86" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 89.86)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are a helpful assistant. Please reason step by step to solve the problem and put the final answer within the &lt;answer&gt;&lt;/answer&gt;tags.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">User:<span id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p2.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> {QUESTION}</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Assistant:<span id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p2.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To encourage the model to place answers within the designated labels, we set the following composite reward function:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R(\cdot)=(1-\beta)\cdot R_{accuracy}(\cdot)+\beta\cdot R_{format}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R(\cdot)=(1-\beta)\cdot R_{accuracy}(\cdot)+\beta\cdot R_{format}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{accuracy}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{accuracy}</annotation></semantics></math> is a binary reward (1 if the final answer is correct, 0 otherwise) from a rule-based verifier. Similarly, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{format}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{format}</annotation></semantics></math> is a binary reward (1 if the specified tags are correctly used, 0 otherwise). We set the weighting coefficient <math id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, we set the sparse reward threshold <math id="A1.SS1.SSS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> (as mentioned in Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Extending GRPO with Adaptive Multi-Guidance Replacement ‣ 3 Adaptive Multi-Guidance Policy Optimization ‣ More Than One Teacher: Adaptive Multi-Guidance Policy Optimization for Diverse Exploration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>). This configuration ensures that adaptive replacement is triggered if and only if every on-policy response in a batch is factually incorrect, regardless of its formatting.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.1.4 </span>Training Hyperparameters</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RL Training.</span> All reinforcement learning experiments were conducted using the VERL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sheng et al. (2024)</a></cite> framework on 4 NVIDIA H100 GPUs, except for the smaller Qwen2.5-1.5B-Ins which used a single NVIDIA H100 GPU. Models were trained for 500 steps using training batch size of 128 and mini-batch size of 64 for updates. For each prompt during rollout, we sampled <math id="A1.SS1.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=8</annotation></semantics></math> responses with a temperature of 1.0 and a maximum response length of 8192 tokens. The optimization used a learning rate of 1e-6, a clipping ratio of 0.2, and an entropy coefficient of 0.001 to encourage exploration. For our AMPO method, the default number of guidance replacements was set to <math id="A1.SS1.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}=2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SFT Training.</span> The supervised fine-tuning (SFT) baseline was trained using the LLaMA-Factory <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al. (2024)</a></cite> library on a single NVIDIA L40 GPU. We employed the LoRA (Low-Rank Adaptation) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al. (2022)</a></cite> technique, applying it to all linear modules of the model. The model was trained for 3 epochs with a learning rate of 5e-5, which was controlled by a cosine learning rate scheduler with a warmup ratio of 0.1. We used batch size of 1 and gradient accumulation steps of 8. Our SFT training was performed using bf16 precision, and the maximum sequence length was capped at 8192 tokens.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Case Studies</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide a comparison of the reasoning processes of the base model, the GRPO-trained model, and the AMPO-trained model on a challenging mathematical problem. This case studies highlights the distinct differences in their problem-solving approaches.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GRPO-trained Model.</span> While the model trained with GRPO shows signs of improved reasoning, such as using reflective phrases like “We need to check…”, its approach remains superficial. It correctly identifies the first scenario for a unique solution, where the derived quadratic equation has exactly one root, but fails to explore other possibilities. This limited depth of reasoning leads it to the same incorrect conclusion as the base model.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AMPO-trained Model.</span> In stark contrast, the AMPO-trained model demonstrates a significantly more sophisticated and robust reasoning process. It exhibits genuine <span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">meta-cognition and self-correction</span>, explicitly identifying a potential flaw in a simplistic approach with the phrase, “There seems to be a misunderstanding…Let’s re-examine…”. Critically, it successfully deconstructs the problem into two distinct cases: (1) the quadratic equation having one valid root, and (2) the quadratic having two roots where only one satisfies the domain constraints of the original logarithmic equation. This comprehensive analysis and deeper deliberation allow it to navigate the problem’s complexity and arrive at the correct solution.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="96.75" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 96.75" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,96.75) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#606060;" fill="#606060" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 90.84 C 0 94.1 2.64 96.75 5.91 96.75 L 544.09 96.75 C 547.36 96.75 550 94.1 550 90.84 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 72.64 L 548.03 72.64 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 81.23)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem Prompt</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:3.15em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="47.05" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 43.59)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Find the number of integer values of <math id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in the closed interval <math id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-500,500]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">500,500</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-500,500]</annotation></semantics></math> for which the equation <math id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(kx)=2\log(x+2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(kx)=2\log(x+2)</annotation></semantics></math> has exactly one real solution. (<span id="A1.SS2.p4.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Answer: 501</span>)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="968.48" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 968.48" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,968.48) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#606060;" fill="#606060" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 962.57 C 0 965.83 2.64 968.48 5.91 968.48 L 544.09 968.48 C 547.36 968.48 550 965.83 550 962.57 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 944.37 L 548.03 944.37 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 952.96)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Response generated by Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:66.15em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="918.79" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 915.33)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To solve the equation <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(kx)=2\log(x+2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(kx)=2\log(x+2)</annotation></semantics></math> and find the number of integer values of <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in the interval <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-500,500]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">500,500</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-500,500]</annotation></semantics></math> for which the equation has exactly one real solution, we will follow these steps:</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. Rewrite the equation using properties of logarithms:<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(kx)=2\log(x+2)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(kx)=2\log(x+2)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Using the property <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(a)=b\log(c)\implies\log(a)=\log(c^{b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(a)=b\log(c)\implies\log(a)=\log(c^{b})</annotation></semantics></math>, we get:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(kx)=\log((x+2)^{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(kx)=\log((x+2)^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. Equate the arguments of the logarithms:<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kx=(x+2)^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kx=(x+2)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3. Expand and rearrange the equation:<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kx=x^{2}+4x+4" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kx=x^{2}+4x+4</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{2}+(4-k)x+4=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{2}+(4-k)x+4=0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4. Analyze the quadratic equation:<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
The quadratic equation <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{2}+(4-k)x+4=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{2}+(4-k)x+4=0</annotation></semantics></math> will have real solutions if its discriminant is non-negative. The discriminant <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> of a quadratic equation <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ax^{2}+bx+c=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ax^{2}+bx+c=0</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=b^{2}-4ac" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=b^{2}-4ac</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Here, <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=4-k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=4-k</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=4</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=(4-k)^{2}-4\cdot 1\cdot 4" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=(4-k)^{2}-4\cdot 1\cdot 4</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=(4-k)^{2}-16" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=(4-k)^{2}-16</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=k^{2}-8k" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=k^{2}-8k</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">5. Determine when the discriminant is non-negative:<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{2}-8k\geq 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{2}-8k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Factor the quadratic expression:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(k-8)\geq 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(k-8)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This inequality holds when <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 8</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">6. Ensure the quadratic equation has exactly one real solution:<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
For the quadratic equation to have exactly one real solution, the discriminant must be zero:</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(k-8)=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(k-8)=0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This gives us two solutions:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0\quad\text{or}\quad k=8" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">or</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0\quad\text{or}\quad k=8</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">7. Check the conditions for these values of <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>:<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.13.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.14.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{2}+4x+4=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{2}+4x+4=0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x+2)^{2}=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x+2)^{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=-2" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=-2</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.15.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">However, <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=-2</annotation></semantics></math> is not in the domain of the original logarithmic equation because <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(x+2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(x+2)</annotation></semantics></math> is undefined for <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=-2</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math> does not provide a valid solution.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.16.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=8</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{2}-4x+4=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{2}-4x+4=0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x-2)^{2}=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x-2)^{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=2" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=2</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.17.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=2</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(8\cdot 2)=2\log(2+2)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(8\cdot 2)=2\log(2+2)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(16)=2\log(4)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(16)=2\log(4)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(16)=\log(16)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(16)=\log(16)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.18.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This is true, and <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=2</annotation></semantics></math> is valid.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.19" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">8. Count the valid integer values of <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>:<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.19.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
The only valid integer value of <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in the interval <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-500,500]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">500,500</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-500,500]</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=8</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.20" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.20.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Therefore, the number of integer values of <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> for which the equation has exactly one real solution is <math id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.21" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.21.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(<span id="A1.SS2.p5.pic1.2.21.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">response tokens: 933, correctness: False</span>)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="1151.13" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 1151.13" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,1151.13) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#606060;" fill="#606060" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 1145.22 C 0 1148.48 2.64 1151.13 5.91 1151.13 L 544.09 1151.13 C 547.36 1151.13 550 1148.48 550 1145.22 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 1127.02 L 548.03 1127.02 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 1135.61)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Response generated by the model trained with GRPO</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:79.35em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="1101.44" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 1097.98)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To find the number of integer values of <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in the interval <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-500,500]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">500,500</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-500,500]</annotation></semantics></math> for which the equation <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(kx)=2\log(x+2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(kx)=2\log(x+2)</annotation></semantics></math> has exactly one real solution, we start by manipulating the logarithmic equation.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Using the properties of logarithms, we can rewrite the equation as:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(kx)=\log((x+2)^{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(kx)=\log((x+2)^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This implies:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kx=(x+2)^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kx=(x+2)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Expanding the right side, we get:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kx=x^{2}+4x+4" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kx=x^{2}+4x+4</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Rearranging terms gives us a quadratic equation:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{2}+(4-k)x+4=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{2}+(4-k)x+4=0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For this quadratic equation to have exactly one real solution, its discriminant must be zero. The discriminant <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> of the quadratic equation <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ax^{2}+bx+c=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ax^{2}+bx+c=0</annotation></semantics></math> is given by <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=b^{2}-4ac" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=b^{2}-4ac</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=4-k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=4-k</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=4</annotation></semantics></math>, so the discriminant is:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=(4-k)^{2}-4\cdot 1\cdot 4=(4-k)^{2}-16" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=(4-k)^{2}-4\cdot 1\cdot 4=(4-k)^{2}-16</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Setting the discriminant to zero for exactly one solution, we have:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(4-k)^{2}-16=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(4-k)^{2}-16=0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This can be rewritten as:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(4-k)^{2}=16" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(4-k)^{2}=16</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Taking the square root of both sides, we get:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4-k=4\quad\text{or}\quad 4-k=-4" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">or</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4-k=4\quad\text{or}\quad 4-k=-4</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Solving these equations, we find:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0\quad\text{or}\quad k=8" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">or</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0\quad\text{or}\quad k=8</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We need to check<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> if these values of <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> indeed give exactly one solution for <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and satisfy the domain restrictions of the original logarithmic equation <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(kx)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(kx)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(x+2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(x+2)</annotation></semantics></math>, which require <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kx&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kx&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+2&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+2&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x&gt;-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&gt;-2</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. For <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the equation becomes:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\cdot x=(x+2)^{2}\implies 0=x^{2}+4x+4\implies(x+2)^{2}=0\implies x=-2" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\cdot x=(x+2)^{2}\implies 0=x^{2}+4x+4\implies(x+2)^{2}=0\implies x=-2</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.13.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">But <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=-2</annotation></semantics></math> is not in the domain <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x&gt;-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&gt;-2</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math> is not a valid solution.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.14.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. For <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=8</annotation></semantics></math>, the equation becomes:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8x=(x+2)^{2}\implies 8x=x^{2}+4x+4\implies x^{2}-4x+4=0\implies(x-2)^{2}=0\implies x=2" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8x=(x+2)^{2}\implies 8x=x^{2}+4x+4\implies x^{2}-4x+4=0\implies(x-2)^{2}=0\implies x=2</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.15.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=2</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.15.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">we check the domain conditions</span>:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kx=8\cdot 2=16&gt;0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kx=8\cdot 2=16&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+2=2+2=4&gt;0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+2=2+2=4&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.16.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Both conditions are satisfied, so <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=8</annotation></semantics></math> is a valid solution.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.17.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Next, <span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.17.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">we need to check</span> if there are any other integer values of <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> that could give exactly one solution.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.18.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For the quadratic equation <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{2}+(4-k)x+4=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{2}+(4-k)x+4=0</annotation></semantics></math> to have exactly one solution, the discriminant must be zero, which we already used to find <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=8</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.19" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.19.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For the quadratic to have no real solutions, the discriminant must be negative:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(4-k)^{2}-16&lt;0\implies(4-k)^{2}&lt;16\implies-4&lt;4-k&lt;4\implies 0&lt;k&lt;8" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(4-k)^{2}-16&lt;0\implies(4-k)^{2}&lt;16\implies-4&lt;4-k&lt;4\implies 0&lt;k&lt;8</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.20" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.20.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We need to check<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.20.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> if any integer <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in the interval <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;k&lt;8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;k&lt;8</annotation></semantics></math> can give exactly one solution. If the quadratic has a negative discriminant, it has no real solutions. If the quadratic has a positive discriminant, it has two distinct real solutions. </span>We need to ensure<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.20.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> there are no other <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> values that can give exactly one solution besides <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=8</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.21" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.21.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in the interval <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m32" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(-500,500]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">500,500</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-500,500]</annotation></semantics></math>, we need to ensure that <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kx=(x+2)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kx=(x+2)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> does not yield another solution for integer <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> other than <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=8</annotation></semantics></math>. The quadratic equation <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{2}+(4-k)x+4=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{2}+(4-k)x+4=0</annotation></semantics></math> will have exactly one solution if and only if the discriminant is zero, which we have already shown happens only for <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=8</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.22" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.22.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Therefore, the only integer value of <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies the condition is <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=8</annotation></semantics></math>. Since we are asked for the number of integer values of <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in the interval <math id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-500,500]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">500,500</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-500,500]</annotation></semantics></math>, and we have found only one such value, the answer is:
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.22.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">&lt;answer&gt;1 &lt;/answer&gt;</span>.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.23" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.23.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(<span id="A1.SS2.p6.pic1.2.23.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">response tokens: 1145, correctness: False</span>)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="1629.89" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 1629.89" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,1629.89) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#606060;" fill="#606060" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 1623.98 C 0 1627.24 2.64 1629.89 5.91 1629.89 L 544.09 1629.89 C 547.36 1629.89 550 1627.24 550 1623.98 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 1605.78 L 548.03 1605.78 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 1614.37)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Response generated by the model trained with AMPO</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:113.95em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="1580.2" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 1576.75)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To solve the equation <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(kx)=2\log(x+2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(kx)=2\log(x+2)</annotation></semantics></math> for integer values of <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in the interval <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-500,500]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">500,500</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-500,500]</annotation></semantics></math> such that the equation has exactly one real solution, we start by manipulating the logarithmic equation.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">First, we rewrite the equation using properties of logarithms:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(kx)=2\log(x+2)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(kx)=2\log(x+2)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This can be rewritten as:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(kx)=\log((x+2)^{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(kx)=\log((x+2)^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Since the logarithmic function is one-to-one, we can equate the arguments:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kx=(x+2)^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kx=(x+2)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Expanding the right side, we get:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kx=x^{2}+4x+4" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kx=x^{2}+4x+4</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Rearranging terms to form a quadratic equation in <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{2}+(4-k)x+4=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{2}+(4-k)x+4=0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For this quadratic equation to have real solutions, the discriminant must be non-negative. The discriminant <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=(4-k)^{2}-4\cdot 1\cdot 4=(4-k)^{2}-16" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=(4-k)^{2}-4\cdot 1\cdot 4=(4-k)^{2}-16</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We need <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(4-k)^{2}-16\geq 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(4-k)^{2}-16\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This inequality can be factored as:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="((4-k)-4)((4-k)+4)\geq 0\implies(-k)(8-k)\geq 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">((4-k)-4)((4-k)+4)\geq 0\implies(-k)(8-k)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">which simplifies to:</span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k-8)k\geq 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k-8)k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The solutions to this inequality are <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 8</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">However, we must also satisfy</span> the domain conditions of the original equation, primarily <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kx&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kx&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x&gt;-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&gt;-2</annotation></semantics></math>. If a solution <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is found, these must hold.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The quadratic equation <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{2}+(4-k)x+4=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{2}+(4-k)x+4=0</annotation></semantics></math> gives the potential solutions. We need exactly one of its roots to be a valid solution to the original logarithmic equation.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. Case 1: The quadratic has one real root (a repeated root).<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
This occurs when the discriminant is zero:</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(4-k)^{2}-16=0\implies(k-4)^{2}=16\implies k-4=\pm 4\implies k=8\text{ or }k=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">±</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"> or </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(4-k)^{2}-16=0\implies(k-4)^{2}=16\implies k-4=\pm 4\implies k=8\text{ or }k=0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.14.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- For <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=8</annotation></semantics></math>, the quadratic is <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{2}-4x+4=0\implies(x-2)^{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{2}-4x+4=0\implies(x-2)^{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, giving the solution <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=2</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.14.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">We check the domain</span>: <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kx=8\cdot 2=16&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kx=8\cdot 2=16&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+2=4&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+2=4&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Both are valid. So, <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=8</annotation></semantics></math> works.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.15.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- For <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the quadratic is <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{2}+4x+4=0\implies(x+2)^{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{2}+4x+4=0\implies(x+2)^{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, giving <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=-2</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.15.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">We check the domain</span>: <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+2&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+2&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is not satisfied. So, <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math> does not work.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. Case 2: The quadratic has two distinct real roots.<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.16.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
This occurs when the discriminant is positive, i.e., <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;8</annotation></semantics></math>. Let the roots be <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. From Vieta’s formulas, the product of the roots is <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}x_{2}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}x_{2}=4</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the product is positive, the two roots must have the same sign. The sum of the roots is <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}+x_{2}=-(4-k)=k-4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}+x_{2}=-(4-k)=k-4</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.17.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- For <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;8</annotation></semantics></math>: The sum <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k-4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k-4</annotation></semantics></math> is positive. Since both the sum and product are positive, both roots <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> must be positive. For each positive root <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, the domain condition <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kx&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kx&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is satisfied (since <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;8</annotation></semantics></math>). The condition <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+2&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+2&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is also satisfied. This means for any <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;8</annotation></semantics></math>, we get two distinct, valid solutions. <span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.17.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">This is not what we want</span>.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.18.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- For <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>: The sum <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k-4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k-4</annotation></semantics></math> is negative. Since the sum is negative and the product is positive, both roots <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> must be negative. <span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.18.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Let’s check</span> the domain for a negative root <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. The condition <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+2&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+2&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> might hold (if <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2&lt;x&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2&lt;x&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>), but the condition <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kx&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kx&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> requires that if <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> must also be negative, which is true for both roots. So for every integer <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have two negative roots, both of which are valid solutions. <span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.18.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">This also gives two solutions, not one</span>.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.19" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">There seems to be a misunderstanding<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.19.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> in the provided text’s reasoning. </span>Let’s re-examine<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.19.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> the problem based on the idea that one of the quadratic’s roots might be invalid. A root <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{2}+(4-k)x+4=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{2}+(4-k)x+4=0</annotation></semantics></math> is only a valid solution to the original equation if <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m52" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+2&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+2&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m53" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kx&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kx&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
A root is invalid if <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m54" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\leq-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\leq-2</annotation></semantics></math> or if <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m55" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kx\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kx\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.20" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.20.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m56" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)=x^{2}+(4-k)x+4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=x^{2}+(4-k)x+4</annotation></semantics></math>.
If the quadratic has two roots, <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m57" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, but only one is valid, that gives one solution.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.21" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.21.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let’s reconsider<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.21.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m58" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. We established both roots <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m59" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are negative.
Product <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m60" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}x_{2}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}x_{2}=4</annotation></semantics></math>. Sum <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m61" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}+x_{2}=k-4&lt;-4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}+x_{2}=k-4&lt;-4</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.22" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.22.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Since the product is 4, neither root can be 0. Since the sum is less than -4, at least one root must be less than -2.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.23" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.23.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let’s check<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.23.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> the value of <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m62" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(-2)=(-2)^{2}+(4-k)(-2)+4=4-8+2k+4=2k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(-2)=(-2)^{2}+(4-k)(-2)+4=4-8+2k+4=2k</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m63" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m64" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(-2)=2k&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(-2)=2k&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. This means <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m65" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2</annotation></semantics></math> lies between the two roots <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m66" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m67" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.24" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.24.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">So, we have <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m68" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}&lt;-2&lt;x_{2}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}&lt;-2&lt;x_{2}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
- The root <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m69" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is invalid because <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m70" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}+2&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}+2&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
- The root <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m71" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is in <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m72" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-2,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-2,0)</annotation></semantics></math>. For this root, <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m73" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}+2&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2}+2&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, since <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m74" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m75" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the product <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m76" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kx_{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kx_{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. So this root is valid.
Therefore, for every integer <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m77" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, there is exactly one valid real solution.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.25" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.25.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">So the valid integer values for <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m78" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> are:
1. <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m79" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=8</annotation></semantics></math> (one value).
2. All integers <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m80" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m81" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. In the interval <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m82" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-500,500]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">500,500</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-500,500]</annotation></semantics></math>, this corresponds to <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m83" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{-500,-499,\dots,-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">500</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">499</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{-500,-499,\dots,-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The number of these integers is <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m84" class="ltx_Math" alttext="500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">500</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">500</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.26" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.26.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The total number of integer values of <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m85" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m86" class="ltx_Math" alttext="500+1=501" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">500</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">501</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">500+1=501</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the number of integer values of <math id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.m87" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is <span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.26.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">&lt;answer&gt;501 &lt;/answer&gt;</span>.</span></span>
<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.27" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.27.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(<span id="A1.SS2.p7.pic1.2.27.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">response tokens: 1826, correctness: True</span>)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
